[size=5][b]Every mod key and controller button, rebindable in the game's own Key Bindings menu.[/b][/size]

One section per installed mod in [b]Settings > Controls > Key Bindings[/b], built at every startup. Rebind everything in one place, with a keyboard or a controller.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
Images: keyboard left, controller right.
[list]
[*][b]One section per mod[/b], named from the mod's files, for example [i]"Mod: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url]"[/i]. Includes keys the mod never made rebindable.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/key-bindings-mod-sections.jpg[/img][/*]
[*][b]Hard-coded game keys rebindable[/b]: Confirm, Cancel, Drop, Disassemble, Unequip, Sell Junk, Preview Item / Add Favorite, Comparison, Track Waypoint, Cycle Objective, map filters and more, on keyboard and controller. On-screen hints follow your keys.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/new-entries.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Controller rebinding[/b], vanilla and mod, per control scheme (Classic, Dynamic, Alternative). The menu shows buttons while you use a controller, keys while you use the keyboard.[/*]
[*][b]Key combinations[/b] on every entry: hold one key or button, press another ([i]"Ctrl + K"[/i], [i]"LB + A"[/i]). On-screen hints show the whole combination.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/combination.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Tap or hold on one key[/b]: a (Hold) action shares its key with another action. Tap for one, hold for the other, for example Crouch (Hold) and Dodge/Dash.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/shared-key.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Conflict warning[/b]: a popup names new conflicts. The side panel lists what the selected key conflicts with, what it is shared with, and every conflicting key. Keys used in different contexts (Jump and the map's Track Waypoint) are not conflicts.
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds/main/screenshots/conflict.png[/img][/*]
[*][b]Unbind[/b] any entry: point at it and press [b]X[/b] (Square on a controller). [b]Defaults[/b] restores it.[/*]
[*][b]Sync[/b] with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], Native Settings UI and Redscript Configuration Framework, both ways.[/*]
[*]Changes apply at once. Keys are stored in a separate file with a backup. No game or mod files are changed.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Supported keybind sources[/b][/size]

[table][tr][th]Status[/th]
[th]Keybind source[/th]
[th]Notes[/th]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] input files (for example [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/5208]Let There Be Flight[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/11765]Enhanced Vehicle System[/url])[/td]
[td]Keys and controller buttons, also ones the mod didn't make rebindable. A mod that registers its file late may appear from the second launch.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url] key options[/td]
[td]Synced both ways. Combinations stay in this menu.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/td]
[td]Hub key (F8) synced with RCF's Options.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28308]Unified Mod Settings[/url][/td]
[td]Single keys. Synced both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#e5be37]2nd launch[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Mods with keys in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]RCF[/url]'s hub, like the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/28390]DigitalVixen[/url] mods[/td]
[td]With the mod's own names. Single keys and controller buttons. Synced both ways.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4008]No More Hard-coded Keybinds[/url][/td]
[td]Covered: every key it adds is an entry. Both can be installed.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b][color=#4caf50]✓ Native[/color][/b][/td]
[td]Vanilla keys and buttons[/td]
[td]The game's own entries, with combinations. Controller layouts per control scheme.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] hotkeys[/td]
[td]Stay in the CET overlay.[/td]
[/tr]
[tr][td][b]⏳ Not yet[/b][/td]
[td]...[/td]
[td]Missing a mod or framework? [b]Leave a comment.[/b][/td]
[/tr]
[/table]
[size=4][b][color=#e5be37]Limitations[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Controller: only actions on exactly one button are listed. Movement, aiming, attacking and sticks stay as they are.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Key combinations apply after a restart, about 30 in total.[/b][/color][/*]
[*][color=#e5be37][b]Map zoom stays on the mouse wheel.[/b][/color][/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url][/*]
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4885]Mod Settings[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/30726]Redscript Configuration Framework[/url][/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Mod Organizer 2, Vortex, or extract into the game folder.

[size=4][b]Uninstallation[/b][/size]
Remove both [font=Courier New]ModKeybindsMenu[/font] folders. Optionally delete [font=Courier New]r6/cache/modkeybinds/[/font] (your mod keys). Nothing is written to your save. Game settings are kept.

[size=4][b]For mod authors[/b][/size]
Any [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4575]Input Loader[/url] action with [font=Courier New]overridableUI[/font], or a [font=Courier New]Button[/font] mapping with a single key or [font=Courier New]buttonGroup[/font], shows up automatically. For nicer names, ship [font=Courier New]r6/config/modkeybinds/<YourMod>.json[/font]:
[code]{
"_section": "Your Mod",
"yourActionName": "Open Menu"
}[/code]
Names can be [font=Courier New]LocKey#...[/font] keys.

[size=4][b]Credits and source[/b][/size]
Uses RED4ext.SDK, pugixml and nlohmann/json. Input manager layouts and address hashes from [url=https://github.com/jackhumbert/mod_settings]Mod Settings[/url]. Source: [url=https://github.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds]github.com/kaporli/unified-keybinds[/url] (MIT).
